From: kosmik2001
Subject: [PATCH] session: start caja with --force-desktop so the desktop is drawn

On this build a plain "caja -n" comes up without managing the desktop when it
starts during the session's early phase (measured on wayfire: no desktop icons
until caja is restarted by the restart loop).  --force-desktop makes caja manage
the desktop regardless of the preferences/environment it reads at startup, which
is also what the X11 session ends up needing here.

--- a/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
+++ b/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 restart_while_running mate-panel &
 restart_while_running polkit-mate-authentication-agent-1 &
 restart_while_running mate-notification-daemon &
 restart_while_running mate-settings-daemon &
-restart_while_running caja -n &
+restart_while_running caja --force-desktop -n &
 
 #Programs to start once (if we have them), matching Xorg behavior
 nm-applet --indicator &
